{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":39486735,"ns":0,"title":"Defensive pessimism","extract":"Defensive pessimism is a cognitive strategy in which an individual sets a low expectation for their performance, regardless of how well they have done in the past. Individuals use defensive pessimism as a strategy to prepare for anxiety-provoking events or performances.","description":"Cognitive strategy for preparation","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}